      "@id": "https://gftd.ai/issue/block-container-node-pattern",
      "name": "Block Container Node Pattern Implementation",
      "description": "Refactored Tiptap nodes to support two patterns: Block Container Nodes (can contain paragraph content) and Inline Atom Nodes (reference tags). Character, Scene, Location, Organization, and POV nodes are now Block Container Nodes. Ghost, Technology, Episode, Arc, Motif, Season, Timeline, Beat, and other reference nodes remain Inline Atom Nodes.",
      "status": "resolved",
      "resolution": "Updated createStoryNode function to support isBlockContainer parameter. Block Container Nodes use group: 'block', content: 'paragraph+', atom: false, and render as div elements with header and content areas. Inline Atom Nodes use group: 'inline', atom: true, and render as span elements. Updated CharacterNode, LocationNode, OrganizationNode, SceneNode, and POVNode to Block Container pattern. Document configuration already supports block+ content."
